### API Throttling Service — full demo walkthrough
###
### Covers the required 2 clients x 2 endpoints x 2 storage strategies matrix.
### Openable directly with the VS Code "REST Client" extension, or copy each
### block out as a curl command. Run the server first (see README.md §2/§3).
###
### client-a: /foo capacity=10 refill=1/s   | /bar limit=5 per 10s window
### client-b: /foo capacity=3  refill=0.2/s | /bar limit=20 per 10s window

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### === Auth failure cases ===

### No Authorization header -> 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/foo

### Unknown client id -> 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/foo
Authorization: bearer nobody

### Malformed scheme -> 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/foo
Authorization: token client-a

### === client-a on /foo (Token Bucket, capacity 10) ===
### Fire this block ~11 times quickly: expect 200 x10, then 429.

GET {{baseUrl}}/foo
Authorization: bearer client-a

### === client-b on /foo (Token Bucket, capacity 3 — throttles much sooner) ===
### Fire this block ~4 times quickly: expect 200 x3, then 429.

GET {{baseUrl}}/foo
Authorization: bearer client-b

### === client-a on /bar (Sliding Window Counter, limit 5 per 10s) ===
### Fire this block ~6 times quickly: expect 200 x5, then 429.

GET {{baseUrl}}/bar
Authorization: bearer client-a

### === client-b on /bar (Sliding Window Counter, limit 20 per 10s) ===
### Fire this block ~21 times quickly: expect 200 x20, then 429.

GET {{baseUrl}}/bar
Authorization: bearer client-b

### === Cross-check: /foo and /bar are independent limits for the same client ===
### After exhausting client-b's /foo above (429), /bar for client-b should still
### return 200 here — proves the two endpoints don't share a counter.

GET {{baseUrl}}/bar
Authorization: bearer client-b

### === Persistence check (STORAGE_DRIVER=redis only) ===
### 1. Run the client-b /foo block above 3x to exhaust its bucket (429 on the 4th).
### 2. Restart the app process (Ctrl-C, `npm start` again) WITHOUT restarting Redis.
### 3. Re-run this request immediately: expect 429 again (state survived the
###    app restart). Repeat the whole check with STORAGE_DRIVER=memory and the
###    same request comes back 200 instead, since in-memory state was wiped.

GET {{baseUrl}}/foo
Authorization: bearer client-b
